
1. weaken on a tied element, bare and as ${\$a[0]}
    STORE[0]=ref
  (the STORE above is the assignment)
  after weaken $a[0]:      tie slot strong
  after weaken ${\$a[0]}: tie slot strong

2. read before the shift, read after
    STORE[0]=10
    STORE[1]=20
    STORE[2]=30
    FETCH[1]
    SHIFT
  via r: 20

3. not read before the shift
    STORE[0]=10
    STORE[1]=20
    STORE[2]=30
    SHIFT
    FETCH[1]
  via r: 30

4. read before, written after the shift
    STORE[0]=10
    STORE[1]=20
    STORE[2]=30
    FETCH[1]
    SHIFT
    STORE[1]=99
    FETCH[0]
    FETCH[1]
    FETCH[1]
  via r: 99; array: 20 99

5. a copy of the reference
    STORE[0]=10
    STORE[1]=20
    STORE[2]=30
    FETCH[1]
    SHIFT
  via r2: 20

6. local, proxy read before
    STORE[0]=10
    STORE[1]=20
    STORE[2]=30
    FETCH[1]
    FETCH[1]
    STORE[1]=undef
    STORE[1]=99
    FETCH[1]
  inside via r: 20; fresh: 99
    STORE[1]=20
    FETCH[1]
  after via r: 20; fresh: 20

7. local, proxy first read inside
    STORE[0]=10
    STORE[1]=20
    STORE[2]=30
    FETCH[1]
    STORE[1]=undef
    STORE[1]=99
    FETCH[1]
    FETCH[1]
  inside via r: 99; fresh: 99
    STORE[1]=20
    FETCH[1]
  after via r: 99; fresh: 20

8. local with a shift inside, proxy read before
    STORE[0]=10
    STORE[1]=20
    STORE[2]=30
    FETCH[1]
    FETCH[1]
    STORE[1]=undef
    STORE[1]=99
    SHIFT
    STORE[1]=20
    FETCH[1]
    FETCH[0]
    FETCH[1]
  after via r: 20; fresh: 20; array: 99 20
